  "asserts_no_claim": true,
  "purpose": "Bind the byte-width zero-entry arm and the yoyo deconfounding by hash before any reviewer reads them.",
  "outcomes_as_reported_scope_carried": {
    "byte_width_arm": "CONFIRMS THE NIBBLE ANALOGUE, FOR M1 AT j0=0 ONLY. At GF(2^8), r=6, four-zero matrix M1, full 2^32 coset: the divisibility-by-256 signature is ABSENT (gcd of nonzero fiber sizes 1, max_occ 12, Poisson histogram), matching the no-zero control arm measured at the same round count. The mechanism OBS-B3-4 named dies between r=5 and r=6 at byte width, and the 32x-vs-2x mod-8 margin gap the BATCH-004 validator flagged did not move the transition round. None of the three preregistered analogue-misled criteria fired.",
    "byte_width_endpoint_discipline": "The producer froze the FIBER-DIVISIBILITY SIGNATURE as the primary endpoint rather than n mod 8, because OBS-B4-2's entailment makes the residue arithmetically certain whenever divisibility is present -- C(256k,2) = 128k(256k-1) -- so the residue carries ZERO information in exactly the case under test, and one 2^32 pass is one trial at the 1/8 level. The verdict rests on the structural endpoint and would be unchanged had the residue landed on 0.",
    "byte_width_scope": "SETTLES THE FOUR-ZERO MATRIX AT ONE INDEX ONLY. M0 at r=6 at byte width is UNMEASURED, and no j0 sweep was run. BATCH-002's r=4 result -- 547608330240 at the critical j0 against exactly 0 at a non-critical one -- shows j0 can matter enormously for zero-entry matrices. r=6 M0, r=7 M1, r=7 M0 and r=7 CTRL were dropped to resource exhaustion, not negative evidence; the binding constraint was an 8 GB array under a 1-thread scatter, not CPU.",
    "deconfounding": "THE S-BOX-TO-S-BOX DIFFERENCE DOES NOT SURVIVE DECONFOUNDING, AND THIS STRENGTHENS THE S-BOX-INDEPENDENCE READING RATHER THAN WEAKENING IT. A fully crossed 3 S-box x 3 seed factorial with the same seed set across all three S-boxes, with pairing VERIFIED (identical key_hex and identical thread_seeds across arms in every block) rather than asserted. S-box main effect p = 0.458. BATCH-004's p = 0.023 re-tested at p = 0.834 WITH THE SIGN REVERSED.",
    "deconfounding_power": "THE NULL IS NOT MERELY UNDERPOWERED. Post-hoc sensitivity, changing no frozen test: had BATCH-004's 11.0x/20.5x been the true S-box rates, the re-test would have rejected with probability 0.816; the 80%-power detectable ratio is about 1.73.",
    "deconfounding_limits": "Two, stated by the producer: the key effect is ALSO null (p = 0.247), so the difference can be said NOT ATTRIBUTABLE TO THE S-BOX but cannot be positively attributed to the key rather than chance -- BATCH-004's p = 0.023 was one uncorrected contrast among three arms. And this does NOT revive the retired headline: three drawn S-boxes still leave CORR-20260803-791ca7's 0.224 lower bound untouched.",
    "structure_destroyed_controls": "Raised to 2^31. All three inside band (AES 1.0x, R1 0.5x, R2 0.5x); the Y-R2-sd 4.0x breach did NOT recur. These arms are tighter than BATCH-004's -- they share seed and armid with their main arms, so each carries the same master key and differs in amask alone. 2^32 was not affordable alongside item 1; 2^31 was preregistered before measuring.",
    "RC_7_reached": "An AES-NI build copying BATCH-002's probe path verbatim agrees with the T-table probe and the plain-Python reference on ALL TEN round counts. This removes the arm-level-implementation-offset explanation for the AES arm."
  },
  "the_gap_this_batch_surfaced_and_did_not_close": {
    "what": "NO ARM IN THIS CAMPAIGN HAS EVER MEASURED THE PRP NULL THAT EVERY EXCESS FACTOR DIVIDES BY. Every 13.5x, 20.5x and 15.63x across five batches rests on an analytic 4 * 2^-32 that has never been checked against a measurement.",
    "found_by": "The deconfounding producer, unprompted, while enumerating RC coverage.",
    "status": "NOT RUN. Named as RC-6's second half."
  },
  "named_as_not_reached": [
